  "guideIntroTitle": "What Loop is",
  "guideIntroBody": "A journal that brings your past thoughts back. Write what's on your mind, set a loop, and the log comes back to you when you chose.",
  "guideWriteTitle": "Write a log",
  "guideWriteBody": "Tap + at the bottom right to write what's on your mind. Attach photos or a video up to 1 minute. Place and weather are saved automatically (turn off in Settings › Location).",
  "guideLoopTitle": "Set a loop — bring it back",
  "guideLoopBody": "Log ⋯ › ↩ Loop. 'Once' brings it back one time (a time based on the forgetting curve is suggested). A notification nudges once; an alarm rings until you dismiss it.",
  "guideRepeatTitle": "Repeating loops",
  "guideRepeatBody": "Choose 'Repeat' in the loop sheet to bring it back every 10 minutes, daily, on weekdays, monthly and more. Each time, a spot to continue the log appears. To end it: ⋯ › Stop loop.",
  "guideFlowTitle": "Continue and view the chain",
  "guideFlowBody": "Write on a log that came back and it joins a chain with a purple line. Use ⋯ › View loop chain to see it from the first log in one line. Tap 'Back to timeline' at the top to return.",
  "guideUpcomingTitle": "Upcoming 7 days",
  "guideUpcomingBody": "Tap the first icon at the top (Upcoming · 7 days) to see every loop coming back in the next 7 days.",
  "guideRhythmTitle": "Morning and evening rhythm",
  "guideRhythmBody": "Past self morning note: at 9 AM, logs from a week, a month and a year ago today. Day wrap-up time: the 'Tonight' chip and nightly loops use this time. Change both in Settings.",
  "guideShareTitle": "Share Loop — to the person next to you",
  "guideShareBody": "Log ⋯ › Share Loop › Send to a nearby device. It goes straight to the phone next to you, with no internet or server. The receiver turns on Settings › Receive from nearby devices. Location is left out by default.",
  "guideBackupTitle": "Backup — export and import",
  "guideBackupBody": "Settings › Export everything saves logs, photos, videos and repeats into one .looplog file. On a new phone, use Settings › Import — logs you already have are skipped. Export now and then.",
